                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>This course systematically covers organic synthesis reactions, organic functional groups, and major types of organic compounds. It teaches the structure, nomenclature, applications, physical and chemical properties, and preparation methods of organic compounds. Special emphasis is placed on the characteristics and mechanisms of important organic synthesis reactions (such as carbonyl condensation reactions, transition metal-catalyzed organic reactions, and pericyclic reactions), as well as the structure, nomenclature, properties, and reactions of skeletal structure types of compounds closely linked to pharmaceuticals and natural products.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
